    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d220">

                <pb facs="0354" n="262" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg262"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Sampson.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-01-31"><hi rendition="#italic">January 31,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 126.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Department’s No. 106, of
                    October 5 last, relative to the summons issued against the United States
                    consul-general at Guayaquil, I inclose copies of two dispatches from that
                    officer, from which it appears that the President of Ecuador has expressed
                    regret at the incident, and that the police magistrate has been removed from
                    office.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>




